// Afrikaans (af) — Indo-European (West Germanic), Latin orthography. Referee: en.wiktionary Afrikaans IPA
// (Wiktionary, HUMAN, 2220 words).. The backbone strips the marks the orthography does
// not determine: STRESS (ˈ ˌ — Afrikaans stress is largely first-syllable but unwritten → we emit none), LENGTH ː
// (the open/closed length is realised by our vowel choice; the referee's ː is redundant), NASALIZATION (ɛ̃ before
// nasal+C — allophonic, deferred), and the diphthong OFFGLIDE tie ( ̯ ). The language folds below neutralise the
// referee's syllable dots, the r~ɾ tap/trill, and the optional-schwa parens. NOT folded: the ə~ɛ/ɪ schwa-reduction of
// UNSTRESSED vowels — that is a real stress-conditioned residual we do not yet model (kept visible, like the Hebrew
// sheva).
